@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il29-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il29-time`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a): an Israeli resident, for an individual, with
--   - paragraphs (1) to (3): the centre of life, the day-count presumptions, their rebuttal;
--   - paragraph (4) and the Regulations of 5766-2006: individuals deemed residents (reg 2) and
--     individuals deemed foreign residents (reg 3);
--   - s 14(b): the adjustment year of a first-time resident or a veteran returning resident.
-- Row IL-29.  The centre of life is evaluative ("מכלול קשריו"): it is an input (a finding, or the five
-- ties named), not a computation.  The day-count tests are exact.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(2): the presumptions`

-- src:ITO:143 | ”תושב ישראל“ או ”תושב“ –
-- src:ITO:144 | (א) לגבי יחיד – מי שמרכז חייו בישראל; ולענין זה יחולו הוראות אלה:
-- src:ITO:151 | (2) חזקה היא שמרכז חייו של יחיד בשנת המס הוא בישראל –
-- src:ITO:152 | (א) אם שהה בישראל בשנת המס 183 ימים או יותר;
-- src:ITO:153 | (ב) אם שהה בישראל בשנת המס 30 ימים או יותר, וסך כל תקופת שהייתו בישראל בשנת המס ובשנתיים שקדמו לה הוא 425 ימים או יותר;
-- src:ITO:154 | לענין פסקה זו, ”יום“ – לרבות חלק מיום;

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a)(2), lines 151-154
GIVEN d0 IS A NUMBER
      d1 IS A NUMBER
      d2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises on` d0 `days in the tax year,` d1 `in the tax year before it and` d2 `in the one before that` MEANS
        d0 AT LEAST 183                                                 -- (a)
    OR  (d0 AT LEAST 30 AND (d0 PLUS d1) PLUS d2 AT LEAST 425)          -- (b)

GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises for` i MEANS
    `a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises on`
        (`the days in Israel in the tax year of` i) `days in the tax year,`
        (`the days in Israel in the tax year before that of` i) `in the tax year before it and`
        (`the days in Israel in the tax year before the one before that of` i) `in the one before that`

§ `Section 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(1) and (3): the finding, the ties, the rebuttal`

-- src:ITO:145 | (1) לשם קביעת מקום מרכז חייו של יחיד, יובאו בחשבון מכלול קשריו המשפחתיים, הכלכליים והחברתיים, ובהם בין השאר:
-- src:ITO:146 | (א) מקום ביתו הקבוע;
-- src:ITO:147 | (ב) מקום המגורים שלו ושל בני משפחתו;
-- src:ITO:148 | (ג) מקום עיסוקו הרגיל או הקבוע או מקום העסקתו הקבוע;
-- src:ITO:149 | (ד) מקום האינטרסים הכלכליים הפעילים והמהותיים שלו;
-- src:ITO:150 | (ה) מקום פעילותו בארגונים, באיגודים או במוסדות שונים;
-- src:ITO:155 | (3) החזקה שבפסקה (2) ניתנת לסתירה הן על ידי היחיד והן על ידי פקיד השומה;

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a)(1), (3), lines 145-155: fork F26 (carried from row IL-08)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it` MEANS
    REFUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a)(3), line 155: fork C2
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the presumption was rebutted and no finding says where the centre of life then is` MEANS
    REFUSE "the presumption was rebutted and no finding says where the centre of life then is: the text does not say that a rebuttal itself places the centre of life outside Israel"

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a)(1), lines 145-150: fork C1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the ties named do not all lie one way, so they do not find the centre of life` MEANS
    REFUSE "the ties named do not all lie one way, so even on the reading that unanimous ties find the centre of life they do not find it"

GIVEN t IS A `Where a tie lies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a tie lies in Israel:` t MEANS t EQUALS `lies in Israel`

GIVEN t IS A `Where a tie lies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a tie lies outside Israel:` t MEANS t EQUALS `lies outside Israel`

GIVEN ties IS A `The ties of an individual`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Where a tie lies`
`the five ties named, as a list:` ties MEANS
    LIST ties's `his permanent home`,
         ties's `where he and his family members live`,
         ties's `his usual or permanent occupation or employment`,
         ties's `his active and material economic interests`,
         ties's `his activity in organisations, unions or institutions`

@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a)(1), lines 145-150: fork C1
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the ties decide the centre of life for` i `under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `ties`
    WHEN `declined where only the ties would decide` THEN
        `no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it`
    WHEN `ties that all lie one way find the centre of life there` THEN
        CONSIDER i's `the ties`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it`
        WHEN JUST ts THEN
            BRANCH
                IF   all `a tie lies in Israel:` (`the five ties named, as a list:` ts)      THEN TRUE
                IF   all `a tie lies outside Israel:` (`the five ties named, as a list:` ts) THEN FALSE
                OTHERWISE `the ties named do not all lie one way, so they do not find the centre of life`

-- Paragraphs (1) to (3) alone: where the centre of life is found, that governs; where it is not, a
-- presumption of paragraph (2) that is not rebutted puts it in Israel.
@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a)(1) to (3), lines 144-155
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(1) to (3): the centre of life is in Israel for` i `under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER i's `the centre of life, as found`
    WHEN JUST w THEN w EQUALS `in Israel`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF   `a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises for` i
        THEN IF   NOT i's `the presumption has been rebutted, by the individual or by the assessing officer`
             THEN TRUE
             ELSE CONSIDER r's `rebuttal`
                  WHEN `declined where a rebutted presumption is the only fact` THEN
                      `the presumption was rebutted and no finding says where the centre of life then is`
                  WHEN `a rebutted presumption finds the centre of life outside Israel` THEN FALSE
        ELSE `the ties decide the centre of life for` i `under` r

§ `Section 14(a): a veteran returning resident`

-- src:ITO:1140 | ”תושב חוזר ותיק“ – יחיד ששב והיה לתושב ישראל לאחר שהיה תושב חוץ במשך עשר שנים רצופות לפחות [note: (לגבי מי שהיה לתושב ישראל בשנות המס 2007–2009, יקראו כאילו נאמר ”חמש שנים רצופות“ במקום ”עשר שנים רצופות“)].

-- "תושב חוזר ותיק" – an individual who became an Israeli resident again after being a foreign resident for ten consecutive years at
-- least; for one who became a resident in the tax years 2007 to 2009, read five consecutive years (the note to the definition).
-- This row uses the definition, not the exemption of s 14(a), which is outside the row.
@ref ITO s 14(a), "תושב חוזר ותיק", line 1140
GIVEN rt IS A `A return to Israel`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(a) — a veteran returning resident:` rt MEANS
    IF   rt's `the tax year in which he became an Israeli resident again` AT LEAST 2007
         AND rt's `the tax year in which he became an Israeli resident again` AT MOST 2009
    THEN rt's `the consecutive tax years he had been a foreign resident before` AT LEAST 5
    ELSE rt's `the consecutive tax years he had been a foreign resident before` AT LEAST 10

§ `Section 14(b): the adjustment year`

-- src:ITO:1141 | (ב)(1) על אף האמור בפסקה (א) להגדרה ”תושב ישראל“ או ”תושב“, לא יראו יחיד שהיה לתושב ישראל לראשונה או לתושב חוזר ותיק, כתושב ישראל, במשך שנה אחת מהמועד שבו עלה או שב לישראל, לפי העניין (בסעיף קטן זה – שנת ההסתגלות), ובלבד שהיחיד הודיע, בתוך 90 ימים מיום הגעתו לישראל כאמור, בטופס שקבע המנהל, על בחירתו בהחלת הוראות סעיף קטן זה.
-- src:ITO:1142 | (2) על אף הוראות פסקה (1), הודיע יחיד על בחירתו בשנת ההסתגלות, כאמור באותה פסקה, תבוא שנת ההסתגלות במניין לעניין התקופות המפורטות להלן:
-- src:ITO:1144 | (ב) התקופה האמורה בפסקה (ב)(2) להגדרה ”תושב ישראל“ או ”תושב“;

-- (1): a first-time resident or a veteran returning resident is not regarded as an Israeli resident for one
-- year from the day he came or returned (the adjustment year), provided he gave notice of the election,
-- on the Director's form, within 90 days of the day he arrived.  (2)(b): if he elected, the adjustment year
-- counts in the ten years of s 1 (b)(2) (the body-of-persons exception, below); (2)(a),(c)-(h) concern
-- other sections and are not in this row.

@ref ITO s 14(b)(1), line 1141: the notice was dated before the day of arrival
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the notice of election is dated before the day of arrival, and the text does not say whether that is within 90 days` MEANS
    REFUSE "the notice of election is dated before the day of arrival, and the text does not say whether that is within 90 days of it"

-- Whether the election was made in time, on each allowed reading of "within 90 days from the day of his arrival".
@ref ITO s 14(b)(1), line 1141: fork N90
GIVEN f IS A `Facts for the adjustment year of section 14(b)`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`the election of the adjustment year was made in time, on the readings allowed, by` f `under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the day he gave notice of the election`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST FALSE
    WHEN JUST nd THEN
        IF   Day nd LESS THAN Day (f's `the day he arrived in Israel`)
        THEN `the notice of election is dated before the day of arrival, and the text does not say whether that is within 90 days`
        ELSE CONSIDER r's `ninety days`
             WHEN `declined where the readings differ` THEN
                 nub (LIST (`days after` AT MOST 90), (`days after` AT MOST 89))
             WHEN `the day of arrival is not counted, so the 90th day after it is in time` THEN LIST (`days after` AT MOST 90)
             WHEN `the day of arrival is the first day, so the 90th day counting it is in time` THEN LIST (`days after` AT MOST 89)
        WHERE
            `days after` MEANS Day nd MINUS Day (f's `the day he arrived in Israel`)

-- Whether section 14(b)(1) displaces paragraph (a) of the definition in the tax year: the values it can take.
@ref ITO s 14(b)(1), line 1141: forks N90 and W
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`section 14(b)(1) displaces paragraph (a) of the definition in the tax year of` i `under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER i's `facts for section 14(b)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST FALSE
    WHEN JUST f THEN
        IF   NOT f's `a first-time resident or a veteran returning resident`
        THEN LIST FALSE
        ELSE nub (concat (map (GIVEN e YIELD map (GIVEN m YIELD e AND m) `the matches`) `the election values`))
        WHERE
            `the election values` MEANS `the election of the adjustment year was made in time, on the readings allowed, by` f `under` r
            `the matches` MEANS
                `the possible matches of the window from` (f's `the day he arrived in Israel`)
                    `to` (`the last day of the window of` 1 `years from` (f's `the day he arrived in Israel`))
                    `, counted as` (JUST 1) `, with` (i's `the tax year`) `under` (r's `windows`)

§ `Regulations of 5766-2006, reg 2: individuals deemed Israeli residents`

-- src:ITO:156 | (4) שר האוצר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע תנאים ולפיהם יראו יחיד שאינו תושב ישראל לפי פסקאות (1) ו־(2) כתושב ישראל, ובלבד שהתקיים בו אחד מאלה:
-- src:ITO:157 | (א) הוא עובד מדינת ישראל;
-- src:ITO:158 | (ב) הוא עובד רשות מקומית בישראל;
-- src:ITO:159 | (ג) הוא עובד הסוכנות היהודית בארץ ישראל;
-- src:ITO:160 | (ד) הוא עובד הקרן הקיימת לישראל, קרן היסוד – המגבית המאוחדת לישראל;
-- src:ITO:161 | (ה) הוא עובד חברה ממשלתית;
-- src:ITO:162 | (ו) הוא עובד רשות ממלכתית או תאגיד שהוקם לפי חוק, וכן רשאי הוא לקבוע כאמור כי סוגי יחידים שרואים אותם כתושבי ישראל לפי פסקאות (1) או (2), לא יראו אותם ככאלה, והכל בתנאים שיקבע;
-- src:RES:20 | סעיף 2 – קביעת יחידים כתושבי ישראל
-- src:RES:21 | יראו כתושב ישראל יחיד שאינו תושב ישראל כאמור בפסקה (א)(4) להגדרה ”תושב ישראל“ או ”תושב“ שבסעיף 1 לפקודה (להלן – ההגדרה), בכל אחד מאלה:
-- src:RES:22 | (1) אם הוא עובד מדינת ישראל – אם יחסי עובד מעביד בינו לבין מדינת ישראל החלו כאשר היה אותו יחיד תושב ישראל;
-- src:RES:23 | (2) אם הוא עובד של מעביד אחר המפורט בפסקה (א)(4) להגדרה – אם יחסי עובד מעביד בינו לבין אותו מעביד החלו כאשר היה היחיד תושב ישראל, ובלבד שלא חלפו חמש שנים מיום שהחל היחיד לעבוד אצל אותו מעביד מחוץ לישראל, והכל אלא אם כן הוכיח אחרת להנחת דעתו של פקיד השומה.

-- Reg 2 applies to "יחיד שאינו תושב ישראל כאמור בפסקה (א)(4)", i.e. one who is not a resident under paragraphs
-- (1) and (2), so it is consulted only where the first test says not resident.

@ref RES reg 2(2), line 23: the five years cannot be tested without the day he began to work abroad
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 2(2) turns on the day he began to work for the employer outside Israel, and it was not given` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 2(2) turns on the day he began to work for that employer outside Israel, and it was not given"

@ref RES reg 2, lines 21-23
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`regulation 2 deems him an Israeli resident, on the readings allowed, in the tax year of` i `under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER i's `employment facts for regulation 2`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST FALSE
    WHEN JUST e THEN
        IF   NOT e's `the individual works for that employer in the tax year`
             OR NOT e's `the employment relationship began while he was an Israeli resident`
        THEN LIST FALSE
        ELSE CONSIDER e's `the employer`
             WHEN `the State of Israel` THEN LIST TRUE                                      -- reg 2(1): no time limit
             WHEN `an employer not named in paragraph (4)` THEN LIST FALSE
             OTHERWISE
                 IF   e's `he proved to the assessing officer that he is not to be deemed a resident`
                 THEN LIST FALSE
                 ELSE CONSIDER e's `the day he began to work for that employer outside Israel`
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN `regulation 2(2) turns on the day he began to work for the employer outside Israel, and it was not given`
                      WHEN JUST d THEN
                          `the possible matches of the window from` d
                              `to` (`the last day of the window of` 5 `years from` d)
                              `, counted as` (JUST 5) `, with` (i's `the tax year`) `under` (r's `windows`)

§ `Regulations of 5766-2006, reg 3: individuals deemed foreign residents`

-- src:RES:26 | יראו יחיד שאינו עולה חדש ושרואים אותו כתושב ישראל כאמור בפסקה (א)(1) ו־(2) להגדרה, כתושב חוץ, אם בחמש שנות המס הקודמות לשנת המס היה תושב חוץ והוא אחד מאלה:
-- src:RES:27 | (1) נציג דיפלומטי או פקיד קונסולרי בשירות סדיר ובתפקיד רשמי של מדינה זרה וכן בן זוגו וילדיו של כל אחד מהם, המתגוררים עמו;
-- src:RES:28 | (2) חייל בצבא מדינה זרה או בשירות האומות המאוחדות;
-- src:RES:29 | (3) יחיד שהגיע לישראל לשם שירות בצבא הגנה לישראל – עד לסיום שירותו הצבאי, אם ביקש שלא להיחשב תושב ישראל;
-- src:RES:30 | (4) סטודנט הלומד בהיקף של חצי תכנית לימודים לפחות – בשלוש השנים הראשונות לשהייתו, בישראל, אם ביקש שלא להיחשב תושב ישראל;
-- src:RES:31 | (5) מורה, מרצה או איש מחקר השוהה בישראל במוסד להשכלה גבוהה או במוסד הוראה אחר ומשמש בתפקיד בעבור אותו מוסד – בשלוש השנים הראשונות לשהייתו בישראל;
-- src:RES:32 | (6) איש דת הממלא תפקיד דתי במוסד דת בישראל על פי הזמנת אותו מוסד – בשלוש השנים הראשונות לשהייתו בישראל;
-- src:RES:33 | (7) חולה המאושפז בבית חולים או במוסד שיקומי שהגיע לישראל לצורך אשפוז או שחלה בעת שהותו בישראל ואשר אילולא תקופת אשפוזו לא היו חלות לגביו הוראות פסקת משנה (א)(2) בהגדרה;
-- src:RES:34 | (8) עיתונאי חוץ וספורטאי חוץ – בחמש השנים הראשונות לשהותם בישראל.

@ref RES reg 3, line 26: the five tax years must be given, oldest first
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 3 asks about exactly five preceding tax years, and the list given has another length` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 3 asks about exactly five preceding tax years, and the list given has another length"

@ref RES reg 3, line 26: fork F5Y
GIVEN f IS A `Facts for regulation 3`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`he was a foreign resident in the five preceding tax years, on the readings allowed, by` f `under` r MEANS
    IF   count (f's `a foreign resident in each of the five preceding tax years, oldest first`) EQUALS 5
    THEN CONSIDER r's `five years`
         WHEN `declined where the readings differ` THEN nub (LIST `every year`, `at least one year`)
         WHEN `he was a foreign resident in every one of the five tax years` THEN LIST `every year`
         WHEN `he was a foreign resident in at least one of the five tax years` THEN LIST `at least one year`
    ELSE `regulation 3 asks about exactly five preceding tax years, and the list given has another length`
    WHERE
        `every year`        MEANS all (GIVEN b YIELD b) (f's `a foreign resident in each of the five preceding tax years, oldest first`)
        `at least one year` MEANS any (GIVEN b YIELD b) (f's `a foreign resident in each of the five preceding tax years, oldest first`)

@ref RES reg 3, lines 29-32, 34: the day of arrival is needed for a window
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 3 runs a window from the day he arrived in Israel, and it was not given` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 3 runs a window from the day he arrived in Israel, and it was not given"

@ref RES reg 3(7), line 33: hospital days are taken out of the days in Israel
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the days of hospitalisation given exceed the days in Israel they are taken from, or are negative` MEANS
    REFUSE "the days of hospitalisation given are negative or exceed the days in Israel they are taken from"

@ref RES reg 3(7), line 33: "אילולא תקופת אשפוזו לא היו חלות לגביו הוראות פסקת משנה (א)(2)"
GIVEN i  IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
      h0 IS A NUMBER
      h1 IS A NUMBER
      h2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a presumption arises for` i `with the hospital days` h0 `,` h1 `and` h2 `taken out` MEANS
    `a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises on`
        (`the days in Israel in the tax year of` i MINUS h0) `days in the tax year,`
        (`the days in Israel in the tax year before that of` i MINUS h1) `in the tax year before it and`
        (`the days in Israel in the tax year before the one before that of` i MINUS h2) `in the one before that`

-- The class of regulation 3, on the readings allowed: the values of "he belongs to the class, for the tax year".
@ref RES reg 3(1) to (8), lines 27-34
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
      f IS A `Facts for regulation 3`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`he belongs, on the readings allowed, to a class of regulation 3 in the tax year of` i `, by` f `under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the class`
    WHEN `a diplomatic representative or consular official of a foreign state in regular service and official capacity, or a spouse or child living with one` THEN LIST TRUE
    WHEN `a soldier of a foreign army or in the service of the United Nations` THEN LIST TRUE
    WHEN `one who came to Israel to serve in the Israel Defense Forces, until the end of his military service` ended asked THEN
        IF   NOT asked
        THEN LIST FALSE
        ELSE CONSIDER f's `the day he arrived in Israel`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN `regulation 3 runs a window from the day he arrived in Israel, and it was not given`
             WHEN JUST d THEN
                 `the possible matches of the window from` d
                     `to` (fromMaybe (YMD 9999 12 31) ended)
                     `, counted as` NOTHING `, with` (i's `the tax year`) `under` (r's `windows`)
    WHEN `a student studying at least half of a programme` asked THEN
        IF   NOT asked
        THEN LIST FALSE
        ELSE `a window of three years from the day he arrived`
    WHEN `a teacher, lecturer or researcher serving a higher-education or other teaching institution` THEN
        `a window of three years from the day he arrived`
    WHEN `a member of the clergy filling a religious post in an institution in Israel at its invitation` THEN
        `a window of three years from the day he arrived`
    WHEN `a hospital patient` came h0 h1 h2 THEN
        IF   NOT came
        THEN LIST FALSE
        ELSE BRANCH
                 IF   h0 LESS THAN 0 OR h1 LESS THAN 0 OR h2 LESS THAN 0
                      OR h0 GREATER THAN `the days in Israel in the tax year of` i
                      OR h1 GREATER THAN `the days in Israel in the tax year before that of` i
                      OR h2 GREATER THAN `the days in Israel in the tax year before the one before that of` i
                 THEN `the days of hospitalisation given exceed the days in Israel they are taken from, or are negative`
                 IF   h0 LESS THAN 1                          -- assumption A5: hospitalised in the tax year itself
                 THEN LIST FALSE
                 OTHERWISE LIST (NOT `a presumption arises for` i `with the hospital days` h0 `,` h1 `and` h2 `taken out`)
    WHEN `a foreign journalist or a foreign athlete as described in section 75A` THEN
        CONSIDER r's `journalist or athlete`
        WHEN `declined where the readings differ` THEN
            nub (append `a window of five years from the day he arrived, as described` (LIST FALSE))
        WHEN `described by what he came to Israel to do, whether or not he is a foreign resident` THEN
            `a window of five years from the day he arrived, as described`
        WHEN `section 75A makes him a foreign resident, so one who is an Israeli resident is not one` THEN LIST FALSE
    WHEN `none of these classes` THEN LIST FALSE
    WHERE
        `a window of three years from the day he arrived` MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `the day he arrived in Israel`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `regulation 3 runs a window from the day he arrived in Israel, and it was not given`
            WHEN JUST d THEN
                `the possible matches of the window from` d
                    `to` (`the last day of the window of` 3 `years from` d)
                    `, counted as` (JUST 3) `, with` (i's `the tax year`) `under` (r's `windows`)
        `a window of five years from the day he arrived, as described` MEANS
            CONSIDER f's `the day he arrived in Israel`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `regulation 3 runs a window from the day he arrived in Israel, and it was not given`
            WHEN JUST d THEN
                `the possible matches of the window from` d
                    `to` (`the last day of the window of` 5 `years from` d)
                    `, counted as` (JUST 5) `, with` (i's `the tax year`) `under` (r's `windows`)

@ref RES reg 3, lines 26-34
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
GIVETH A LIST OF BOOLEAN
`regulation 3 deems him a foreign resident, on the readings allowed, in the tax year of` i `under` r MEANS
    CONSIDER i's `facts for regulation 3`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST FALSE
    WHEN JUST f THEN
        IF   f's `a new immigrant within section 35(d)`
        THEN LIST FALSE
        ELSE nub (concat (map (GIVEN y YIELD map (GIVEN c YIELD y AND c) `the class values`) `the five-year values`))
        WHERE
            `the five-year values` MEANS `he was a foreign resident in the five preceding tax years, on the readings allowed, by` f `under` r
            `the class values`     MEANS `he belongs, on the readings allowed, to a class of regulation 3 in the tax year of` i `, by` f `under` r

§ `The readings by default`

@ref this row; Meng's ruling SHRUG of 2026-10-08: every fork declines by default
GIVETH A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
`the default readings of row IL-29` MEANS
    `The readings of the forks of row IL-29` WITH
        `ties`                       IS `declined where only the ties would decide`
        `rebuttal`                   IS `declined where a rebutted presumption is the only fact`
        `windows`                    IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `five years`                 IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `ninety days`                IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `journalist or athlete`      IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `years deemed`               IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `partial day`                IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `both statuses`              IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `part-year connection`       IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `midpoint`                   IS `declined where the midpoint decides`
        `excess deduction`           IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `old schedule`               IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `depreciation base`          IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `part month`                 IS `declined where the readings differ`
        `part month of depreciation` IS `declined where the readings differ`

§ `Section 1 "Israeli resident" (a), the whole of it`

@ref ITO s 14(b): the readings of the 90 days and of the window differ
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 14(b) may or may not displace the definition in this tax year, depending on the 90 days or on how its year is matched with the tax year` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 14(b) may or may not displace the definition in this tax year: the text does not say how the 90 days run or how the adjustment year is matched with a tax year that it overlaps"

@ref RES reg 3: the readings differ
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 3 may or may not deem him a foreign resident in this tax year, depending on a reading the text does not decide` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 3 may or may not deem him a foreign resident in this tax year: the text does not decide how a window of years is matched with a tax year, whether all five preceding tax years or only one must be foreign residence, or whether a foreign journalist or athlete must already be a foreign resident"

@ref RES reg 2: the readings differ
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 2 may or may not deem him an Israeli resident in this tax year, depending on how its five years are matched with the tax year` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 2 may or may not deem him an Israeli resident in this tax year: the text does not say how the five years from the day he began to work outside Israel are matched with the tax year"

@export Whether an individual was an Israeli resident in a tax year from 2024 under Income Tax Ordinance s 1 "Israeli resident" (a): the centre of life found, or the presumptions of paragraph (2) by days in Israel; with the Regulations of 5766-2006 (regs 2 and 3) and s 14(b)'s adjustment year; each fork of the text declines by default
@ref ITO s 1, "תושב ישראל" (a), lines 143-163; RES regs 2 and 3; ITO s 14(b), line 1141
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
          @desc the three tax years (this one and the two before it), the days in Israel (counted by the caller, or from the stays), any finding of where the centre of life is, the five ties named, whether a presumption was rebutted, and the facts of regulations 2 and 3 and of s 14(b) where they may reach him
      r IS A `The readings of the forks of row IL-29`
          @desc the reading of each fork; every field set to its declining default answers where the readings agree and declines where they differ
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 "Israeli resident" (a): an Israeli resident in the tax year of` i `under` r MEANS
    `for` (i's `the tax year`) `, row IL-29 answers`
        (IF   all (GIVEN a YIELD a) `section 14(b) values`
         THEN FALSE
         ELSE `the single value among` `all values` `, else` `why they differ`)
    WHERE
        `section 14(b) values` MEANS `section 14(b)(1) displaces paragraph (a) of the definition in the tax year of` i `under` r
        base MEANS `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(1) to (3): the centre of life is in Israel for` i `under` r
        `regulation 3 values` MEANS IF base THEN `regulation 3 deems him a foreign resident, on the readings allowed, in the tax year of` i `under` r ELSE LIST FALSE
        `regulation 2 values` MEANS IF base THEN LIST FALSE ELSE `regulation 2 deems him an Israeli resident, on the readings allowed, in the tax year of` i `under` r
        `all values` MEANS
            concat (concat (map (GIVEN a YIELD
                                   map (GIVEN c YIELD
                                          map (GIVEN b YIELD IF a THEN FALSE ELSE IF base THEN NOT c ELSE b) `regulation 2 values`)
                                       `regulation 3 values` )
                                `section 14(b) values`))
        `why they differ` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF   count (nub `section 14(b) values`) GREATER THAN 1
                THEN `section 14(b) may or may not displace the definition in this tax year, depending on the 90 days or on how its year is matched with the tax year`
                IF   count (nub `regulation 3 values`) GREATER THAN 1
                THEN `regulation 3 may or may not deem him a foreign resident in this tax year, depending on a reading the text does not decide`
                OTHERWISE `regulation 2 may or may not deem him an Israeli resident in this tax year, depending on how its five years are matched with the tax year`
